ttleships. When the age of knights ends, you decide whether to lead the new age or refuse it.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/2aad5379e695af85f3b97ba772b0b929.poster.avif?t=1786523782\" width=1170 height=658 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/2aad5379e695af85f3b97ba772b0b929.webm?t=1786523782\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/2aad5379e695af85f3b97ba772b0b929.mp4?t=1786523782\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/d12057963a992edd5957fb6300d26d52.avif?t=1786523782\" width=780 height=86 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Every rumor in this world travels through conversation, and you can start one. Praise an ally to strengthen your faction. Repair your standing with resentful vassals. Whisper about a rival king to his own nobles and watch his realm split. Or broker peace between two crowns before the war starts at all.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Information moves the same way. Whoever you are hunting, whatever you are looking for, the trail starts with a drink in a tavern.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/8b9855484a01ce2dfcea1e16104df8c2.avif?t=1786523782\" width=1548 height=771 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/941d503c4d5f054ec13c77315e3ea65a.avif?t=1786523782\" width=780 height=86 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Everything above is also true for every NPC in the world. They earn renown, take service, win fiefs, found factions, marry, and rebel, whether you are watching or not. But not everyone here wants a crown. Each is chasing a goal of their own: some want power, others just want their nation, or their people, to endure.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Relationships work the same way too. Grow close to someone, and their friends warm to you while their enemies mark you as one of them. This web binds NPCs to each other just as it binds them to you.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >And death is never the end of a story. Kill someone in battle and their family and closest friends will remember exactly who did it. Settle that vendetta with another death, and it doesn't end there: it becomes someone else's grudge to carry. The feud that ends your campaign may be several deaths removed from the one that started it, between people who never met.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/0c9b337ad80b8f613434c35f9149213f.avif?t=1786523782\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras_big/0c9b337ad80b8f613434c35f9149213f.webp?t=1786523782 width=1560 height=785 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/61817f9fce2a377e19050e7eb66ac4dd.avif?t=1786523782\" width=780 height=86 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >You are the last of the long-lived. With his dying breath, the old man who raised you gave you your purpose: watch history, and keep it from ending. As wars drag on and grudges accumulate between nations and people, the world's Collapse advances. Let it reach its limit, and history itself ends.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The task itself never changes, whatever you choose to do with your life. What grows as you rise, as a vassal lord, a king, or the power behind one, is how much you can actually do about it: end wars through diplomacy, narrow the gap between your richest fiefs and your poorest, crush the warmongers by force, or quietly turn old enemies into friends. A world with full granaries, safe roads, libraries, and parliaments grows tolerant, and tolerance slows the Collapse.<br> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The dilemma is that living in this world feeds it. The revenge you are owed advances the Collapse. The war that wins you a crown advances it faster. Every character around you is pursuing their own ends inside the same constraint, and their choices weigh as much as yours.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/0557708801db1f70e446a7f17305bbbf.avif?t=1786523782\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras_big/0557708801db1f70e446a7f17305bbbf.webp?t=1786523782 width=1560 height=604 /></span></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/a04f05a079c8e48c5527153fd5001a53.avif?t=1786523782\" width=780 height=86 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >At the center of this world stands the Obelisk: a vast structure said to have once held limitless knowledge. What it is, and what it has to do with the Collapse, is yours to find out.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/4b09dbe4a81906f47264c32019a11fcc.avif?t=1786523782\" width=1560 height=806 /></span></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/2953520/extras/189a9889338c6f89e95a5ccc8911a27f.avif?t=1786523782\" width=780 height=86 /></span></h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >There is no predetermined scenario in this game.<br>The &quot;history that is observed&quot; through countless events becomes a story that is yours alone.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u>&quot;My spouse died in battle. I went to war to avenge them, and by the end of my revenge, the world had collapsed.&quot;</u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u>&quot;I never took a crown. I spent twenty years as the right hand of an NPC I believed in, and together we unified the continent.&quot;</u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><u>&quot;I executed every prisoner from every kingdom I conquered. Their families remembered. The declarations of vengeance never stopped coming.&quot;</u></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >These are all one-of-a-kind stories experienced by real players.<br>A different history unfolds every playthrough, leaving you thinking <strong>&quot;I want to try this differently next time&quot;</strong> even after dozens of hours.</p>",
        "short_description": "A medieval sandbox. Serve a king, rule your own fief, or raise a claimant to the throne. Marry, scheme, rebel, claim a crown, or just watch. Every NPC in this world lives by the same rules you do, driving it toward collapse. Stopping it is your task; the higher you rise, the more ways you have.",
        "supported_languages": "English, Japanese, Simplified Chinese, Traditional Chinese",
        "reviews": "“What this game weaves is a single sweeping saga. This is not a game played for the visceral pleasures of realistic or exhilarating combat, or of a story that moves you to tears. Each individual action, whether by the player or an NPC, is nothing more than the babbling of a small stream. As you near the river's mouth, the channel widens, and before you know it, it has swelled into a great, surging current. The runaway momentum of a world come unhinged is something no one can stop, and it seems, in itself, like a living thing.”<br>ファミ通（Famitsu）<br>",
